steriet Where to Submit an Application VFS Global. The Visa Application Centres offer you: A fast and convenient service; No or little queuing; Copy and photo service available at a fee; Advice on ho... 9 sites To link your passport to your approved New Zealand Parental Residence Visa, you must submit it to the New Zealand Visa Application Centre (NZVAC) operated by VFS Global in Pretoria. Because you are couriering it from Bonnievale, you must pay the VFS passport handling fee and optional return courier fees before shipping your package. VFS Global Step 1: Prepare Your Document Package Pack your documents securely in a sealed envelope, including: Your Original Passport (Must be valid and have blank pages). The Approval / Passport Request Letter received from Immigration New Zealand. Proof of Payment for the VFS Global Passport Handling Fee (and return courier fee if chosen). Completed VFS Payment Form (with credit card authorization if you did not do a direct bank transfer). Contact Information Sheet listing your full name, email address, phone number, and physical return address in Bonnievale. Step 2: Pay VFS Global Fees Online You cannot send the passport without paying the processing fee first. VFS Global Visit the VFS Global New Zealand South Africa portal to find the current bank account details or download their credit card authorization form. VFS Global +1 Pay the mandatory Passport Handling Fee. Note on Return Delivery: It is highly recommended to pay the extra VFS Courier Passback Fee. This ensures VFS will automatically use their secure partner network to ship your passport back to Bonnievale once the visa is linked. Step 3: Courier the Package to VFS Pretoria Since Bonnievale does not have a physical VFS branch, you will need to use a reliable local courier service (such as PostNet, DHL, or The Courier Guy) to send your package to the main processing hub. Address the shipment exactly to: New Zealand Visa Application Centre VFS Global Brooklyn Pavilion, 316 Tram Street Nieuw Muckleneuk, Brooklyn Pretoria 0181 Ensure you opt for a secure hand-delivery service with a tracking number so you can track its arrival at the Pretoria hub. Step 4: Tracking and Return Once received, VFS Pretoria will process your passport and transmit the physical details to link your visa. If you paid for the VFS return courier service, they will generate a tracking number and dispatch it back to your Bonnievale address as soon as Immigration New Zealand clears it. Would you like me to help you find the exact VFS bank account details for the transfer, or do you need the current fee amounts for the passport handling service</div></div></div></button><div class="MW5ipb"><div class="Mx0qM"></div><div class="zIRyqe"><div id="actions-button-Ta-Aau-DH865hbIP5ZfUkAM" data-ved="0CC0QwqUQahcKEwiQ17fu5L-WAxUAAAAAHQAAAAAQFg" data-hveid="45"><div class="YHsVn" data-ved="0CC4QkK0UahcKEwiQ17fu5L-WAxUAAAAAHQAAAAAQFg"><button role="button" aria-label="more options for The main VFS Global Visa Application Centre in Pretoria is located at Brooklyn Pavilion, 316 Tram Street, Nieuw Muckleneuk, Brooklyn, Pretoria, 0181. This location handles standard walk-ins, document submissions, and return passport courier setups. Centre Details &amp; Operations Address: Brooklyn Pavilion, 316 Tram Street, Nieuw Muckleneuk, Brooklyn, Pretoria, 0181 Hours: Monday to Friday, 08:00 â€“ 17:00 (Submission and collection times vary by specific country guidelines) Service Type: Standard document drop-off, biometric enrollment, and optional return courier services processed directly through their partnered courier network. If you need help tracking a specific delivery or want to confirm if your visa category uses a different collection office, please share the country you applied to or your tracking reference type. VFS Global Pretoria | vfsglobal Pretoria. This Visa Application Centre has an additional fee requirement. Service Fee: ZAR 513. Service fee is inclusive of VAT. Mode of Pa