w-zealand-active-faults-map/&quot;,null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[{&quot;1218&quot;:[16]}]],16,null,&quot;New Zealand Active Faults map - GNS Science&quot;,&quot;Both datasets comprise polylines that represent the location of an active fault trace at or near the surface, at different scales. Each fault trace has attributes that describe its name, sense of movement, displacement, recurrence interval and other parameters. The high-resolution dataset group on the GNS webmap also includes two polygon layers derived from the NZAFD: Fault Avoidance Zones, which delineate areas of surface rupture hazard, as defined by the Ministry for the Environment Active Fault Guidelines (Kerr et al. 2003 ), or modifications thereof. Fault Awareness Areas, which highlight areas where a surface rupture hazard may exist (Barrell et al. 2015 ) and where more work is needed.&quot;,&quot;https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q\u003dtbn:ANd9GcTGD_Kvp2RJ0cAB-UmtW8M6qISWULVx9LAlRV0D5zI_vTert-6G8bHB20G_Aw6tVgpiNlJVmChxTWWE5tY&quot;,&quot;GNS Science&quot;,&quot;https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url\u003dhttps://www.gns.cri.nz\u0026client\u003dAIM\u0026size\u003d128\u0026type\u003dFAVICON\u0026fallback_opts\u003dTYPE,SIZE,URL&quot;,[[1787798900246729,4281273,1359493009],null,null,null,null,[[1,3,28]]],null,&quot;3123ecb1-6375-47a5-824e-b69520381465&quot;]]--></span>.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></span><span jsuid="p06onf_4f" class="WBgIic notranslate" jsaction="rcuQ6b:&amp;p06onf_4f|npT2md" jscontroller="XqmSxe#JjQTXe" data-sfc-root="ep" data-wiz-uids="p06onf_4g,p06onf_4h,p06onf_4i" data-complete="true" data-sfc-inited="2"><span class="NMq1me" data-animation-atomic="" jsaction="click:&amp;p06onf_4f|ZUljYd"><span aria-hidden="true"> </span><!--qkimaf p06onf_4f/HugV6--><!--cqw1tb p06onf_4f/HugV6--><button jsuid="p06onf_4h" tabindex="0" data-amic="true" data-icl-uuid="88d0eff9-fd30-4ef8-85a8-d0e72c9e46ed" aria-label="Related results" class=